---
title: "2. An import, end to end — one successful attempt"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Caller service
  participant API as API + Lambda
  participant D as DynamoDB
  participant Q as imports queue
  participant W as Import worker
  participant S as S3

  C->>API: POST /jobs — kind, inputKey, idempotencyKey
  API->>D: conditional PutItem keyed by idempotency key<br/>status=queued, attempt=0, version=1
  Note over API,D: Deliberately not a GSI lookup: index reads are never<br/>strongly consistent, so two concurrent submissions<br/>with one key would both miss and create two jobs
  D-->>API: condition passed — the job exists exactly once
  API->>Q: SendMessage carrying only { jobId }
  API-->>C: 202 Accepted + jobId

  Q->>W: ReceiveMessage { jobId }
  W->>D: GetItem with ConsistentRead
  D-->>W: status=queued, version=v
  W->>D: UpdateItem status=running, attempt=n+1, lease<br/>condition: version = v
  D-->>W: claim won — version = v+1
  Note over W: If that condition had failed, another worker owns<br/>the job and this one returns its message<br/>without converting. That is duplicate delivery, solved.

  W->>W: convert in-process, under the 15-minute deadline

  Note over W,S: OBJECT FIRST, RECORD SECOND — the record can<br/>never advertise bytes that do not exist
  rect rgb(213, 242, 218)
    W->>S: PutObject imports/{id}/attempts/{n}/result.json
    S-->>W: durable — and immutable, because the key is per attempt
    W->>D: UpdateItem status=succeeded, outputKey<br/>condition: version = v+1
    D-->>W: committed — the single atomic moment a result becomes THE result
  end

  W->>Q: DeleteMessage — ack
  C->>API: GET /jobs/{id}
  API-->>C: succeeded + outputKey — or the webhook fires off the same transition
